# E876 collaborator draft; formal ID subject to editor review.
id: E876
trigger_tool: make|shunit2|bash
phase: testing
error_signature: FAILED \(failures=[1-9][0-9]*\)|[0-9]+ tests, [1-9][0-9]* failures, 0 skipped
severity: 2
category: testing, shell, detection
match_keywords: make test, shunit2, tests/runner, tee, failures=4, unace, unrar, exit 0
title: Upstream shunit2 runner pipes suites to tee and reports failure while make test exits zero
root_cause: The shell runner pipes each shunit2 suite to tee, discarding suite exit status; it prints failed assertions without returning nonzero, so absent optional unace/unrar tools cause make test to return zero despite real failures.
affected_scope: Bash/shell projects using shunit2 runners with suite output piped to tee and conditional external format tools.
verification_cmd: make test > upstream.log 2>&1; rc=$?; grep -E 'FAILED \(failures=|tests, [0-9]+ failures' upstream.log; printf 'make_rc=%s\n' "$rc"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: inspect-shunit-summary-and-dependencies
rec_description: >
  Count the real test cases and failing cases from each Ran/FAILED/OK block,
  check optional commands for the failed formats, and report both actual
  assertion failures and the misleading make exit status. Do not claim a pass.
rec_command: grep -E 'Ran [0-9]+ tests|FAILED \(failures=|^OK$|tests, [0-9]+ failures' upstream.log
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual-upstream-test-audit
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: test-mandatory-formats-separately
fallback_description: Execute only available formats in a separate consumer test, keeping missing optional formats marked unverified.
fallback_command: command -v unace; command -v unrar; command -v 7z
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-test-separation
forbid_1_pattern: make test.*exit 0.*all pass
forbid_1_reason: The runner's tee pipeline and final summary return 0 even when shunit2 reports failures.
forbid_1_consequence: Inflated upstream pass rate; hidden lack of external extractors.
principles: P016
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
